                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Son of John Courtenay (q.v.) 1738-1816. </p>
                        <p>Ed Pope notes: Kenneth son of John Courtenay DNB 1738-1816. He died
                            26.4.1838 aged 69 and lived his last years in Florence but he could have
                            been the 1821 entries with no initial after his father's death. The 1812
                            entry above could have been his father but more likely Kenneth as he was
                            at Walking Stewart's again a few Sundays later </p> <p>We have treated K Courtney and K Courtenay as the same person.</p>
